WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:07.280
Welcome to CSC-244, Android Development With Kotlin, taught by Professor Harris

2
00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.340
Williams at Bunker Hill Community College.

3
00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:13.180
You'll turn your programming experience into apps people can use.

4
00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:18.210
This course is fully online and asynchronous, with one module every

5
00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:21.470
week. You'll build interfaces, connect front ends to back ends, and

6
00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:24.170
explore authentication, security, publishing, and monetization.

7
00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:28.130
You'll prototype screens for touch and keyboard input, use GET and

8
00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:32.250
POST requests, manage permissions, and plan transfers around connectivity and battery

9
00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.250
life. Here's how your skills will grow.

10
00:00:36.025 --> 00:00:40.125
Kotlin Basics introduces decisions, loops, collections, and classes.

11
00:00:40.945 --> 00:00:43.985
In Creating Your First App, you'll set up Android Studio and

12
00:00:43.985 --> 00:00:47.365
run an app. Working With the UI Editor connects screen controls

13
00:00:47.365 --> 00:00:48.485
to your Kotlin code.

14
00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:55.840
Next, Activities and Intents covers navigation, lifecycle changes, and Logcat debugging.

15
00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:59.580
UI in Depth adds styles, drawables, and animation.

16
00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.640
Menus and Lists helps you organize actions and repeated items.

17
00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:09.630
Saving and Loading Data keeps information available when an app reopens.

18
00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:13.010
Background Tasks explores responsive interfaces.

19
00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:17.690
Then Volley introduces requests that bring web API data into your

20
00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:17.890
app.

21
00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:24.320
Notifications helps you create useful alerts, while Camera covers taking and

22
00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:28.500
saving photos. In Module 12, Work on the Note-Taking App Project

23
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:31.860
brings your skills together in a Note-Taking App connected to a

24
00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:32.580
REST API.

25
00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:38.990
Deployment explores publishing and your final-project proposal and prototype in Module

26
00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:44.310
13. Beyond Android Studio compares backend services and other mobile approaches.

27
00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:47.910
Module 15, Work on the Final Project, gives you room to

28
00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:50.050
create an app that solves a problem you choose.

29
00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:53.410
So, what does a week look like?

30
00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:56.610
Review the slides, watch the videos, read, and practice.

31
00:01:57.410 --> 00:02:00.390
Each module has a graded discussion about real-world apps.

32
00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:04.710
Assignments are not required for every module; the assigned app mini-projects

33
00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:05.650
grow in complexity.

34
00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:09.230
Now let's find your materials.

35
00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:11.970
In Canvas, select Modules in the course menu.

36
00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:16.650
Learning Materials contains your preparation; Deliverables contains the graded work.

37
00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:21.410
No textbook is required. Module one uses Jupyter notebooks; other modules

38
00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:24.150
list the videos and readings assigned in the course plan.

39
00:02:26.075 --> 00:02:29.355
Select Grader Than in the course menu to reach Workspace for

40
00:02:29.355 --> 00:02:32.175
basic Kotlin demonstrations and server examples.

41
00:02:32.915 --> 00:02:36.575
For general app development, you must install Android Studio on your

42
00:02:36.575 --> 00:02:41.550
computer. Your app assignments do not use the Grader Than autograder.

43
00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:45.450
Upload a video of yourself using your app to its Canvas

44
00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:49.330
assignment. Use feedback to improve it, and resubmit as many times

45
00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:50.910
as you like until the end of class.

46
00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:54.830
Start early, leave time to test, and ask questions when you're

47
00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:57.150
stuck. I look forward to seeing what you create!

